{"agent_id":"pp3g-Zbk6-implementation-task-for-issue-350-implement-the-349","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-08-10T15:39:08.318443006Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"84644164-9cf0-41db-bb30-ca704b67b6d2","comment_uuid":"07192a79-c957-48d3-ab8c-2e7316ae4fff","author":"pp3g-Zbk6-implementation-task-for-issue-350-implement-the-349","content":"Result: #349 cleanup rescope implemented + verified.\n\nFORK (commit 37789b51, branch feature/pp3g-Zbk6-cleanup-rescope-349, NOT pushed):\n- cleanup.rs: --only <id1,id2,...> selective mode (comma-separated, clap value_delimiter) — resolves IDs by exact id / driver--slug / worktree dir name; errors on unknown IDs (fail-closed); refuses Active (running) agents; mutually exclusive with --force and --keep.\n- Blanket --force is now OPERATOR-ONLY via env gate (design choice: option (a)+(c) — the flag remains in the CLI but bails unless CROSSLINK_OPERATOR=1, which agent launches never have; structurally impossible for an agent to bulk-delete STALE agents, the #227 incident class). Gate fires before planning/printing.\n- Non-force DONE path kept; every non-dry-run removal prints the full blast radius and requires confirmation: --yes or interactive [y/N]; --json requires --yes (no silent non-interactive removal).\n- Extraction: plan_cleanup / resolve_only_agents / operator_gate_ok / cleanup_with_agents (injectable confirmer) — pure, unit-testable. 11 new tests added.\n- CLI: --only, --yes flags in main.rs; dispatch updated in mod.rs.\n\nVERIFICATION:\n- cargo build OK. Full bin suite: 2909 passed, 0 failed (incl. 11 new cleanup tests + 215 kickoff tests).\n- CLI smoke tests (temp harness, fake worktrees in /tmp only): --force w/o env refused with operator-only error; --force w/ env reaches STALE sweep; --only removes exactly the named agents; --only unknown → not-found error; --only+--force/--keep mutual exclusion; declined confirmation executes nothing; interactive 'y' proceeds; --json w/o --yes refused.\n\nPERMISSIONS (ASES commit a92fc845, branch feature/pp3g-Zbk6-implementation-task-for-issue-350-implement-the-349):\n- orchestrator.md bash allowlist += 'git worktree remove *' and 'tmux kill-session *' (bounded per-path/-name; no wildcards beyond the single arg); new BOUNDED PER-ID REMOVAL section documenting exact-match-only, no --all/globs, no cleanup --force.\n- hook-config.json by_type.orchestrator.gated_git_commands += 'git worktree remove' (active-issue gate, same pattern as git commit/merge — verified in crosslink-guard.ts section 4). tmux kill-session is NOT in the pass-through allowed_bash, so it is gated on active issue by strict-mode enforcement (guard sections 9-10).\n- permissions.md snapshot updated to match.\n- AGENT SURFACES: reviewer/auditor bash allowlists contain no kickoff/cleanup entries at all (verified by grep); builder can type the command but the binary refuses it without CROSSLINK_OPERATOR — the guarantee is structural, per #349 operator direction.\n- Docs updated: SESSION-END.md, crosslink-subagent-orchestration.md, agent-orchestration-playbook.md (playbook is a 5.5-mirrored file).\n\nTRIPN-ASTRO MIRROR (commit e2e5dd5f, per 5.5): orchestrator.md + hook-config.json by_type + playbook cleanup references updated identically.\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: the opencode guard-layer behavior (by_type gating of git worktree remove) was verified by code-reading the plugin, not by live opencode execution; requires an opencode restart to take effect (permissions.md note 5). Nothing was pushed (per hard rules).","created_at":"2026-08-10T15:39:08.310267153Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:flauJlf98TnWtPZmGTAWR7XXasiVgqG69rxc14Tr3Y4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgqS0OpAYw7klbcxZ96bMZtSHOJRst07xBtXVQQpMDkH4AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAkxw+Y1yQhUtO9IQZusqHNo70TIShe726A6ezMUZyGdEd6yo+w4/tP8Ar1G1OgLWe70piBHjHUVPEmHiCpUEuDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:flauJlf98TnWtPZmGTAWR7XXasiVgqG69rxc14Tr3Y4","signature":"